WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:15.561
Bobbie waited with the boy in the dark tunnel.

2
00:00:16.521 --> 00:00:17.722
The candle was almost out.

3
00:00:18.883 --> 00:00:20.043
Finally the boy woke up.

4
00:00:20.064 --> 00:00:23.826
"Oh! I'm glad you woke up," said Bobbie.

5
00:00:23.846 --> 00:00:26.088
"Please don't faint again!

6
00:00:26.928 --> 00:00:27.629
What's your name?"

7
00:00:27.649 --> 00:00:29.850
"Jim," he said.

8
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.344
"My name's Bobbie," she said.

9
00:00:33.364 --> 00:00:35.825
"But you're a girl, aren't you?"

10
00:00:36.225 --> 00:00:36.766
he asked.

11
00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:40.027
"Yes, my real name is Roberta.

12
00:00:41.047 --> 00:00:43.188
I wish I were a boy, though," said Bobbie.

13
00:00:43.208 --> 00:00:45.909
"My brother and sister went to get help."

14
00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.671
"Why didn't you go with them?"

15
00:00:49.051 --> 00:00:49.611
Jim asked.

16
00:00:49.631 --> 00:00:53.072
"Someone had to stay with you," Bobbie said.

17
00:00:53.092 --> 00:00:56.234
"Well, Bobbie, you're very brave!"

18
00:00:56.694 --> 00:00:57.154
said Jim.

19
00:00:57.174 --> 00:01:03.248
"The candle is out," said Bobbie.

20
00:01:03.268 --> 00:01:04.809
"Are you afraid of the dark, Bobbie?"

21
00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:05.750
asked Jim.

22
00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.872
"No, not very afraid," said Bobbie.

23
00:01:08.892 --> 00:01:13.255
"But "Let's hold hands," said Jim kindly.

24
00:01:14.236 --> 00:01:16.518
He put his big hand over her small hand.

25
00:01:17.518 --> 00:01:18.439
They sat and waited.

26
00:01:21.341 --> 00:01:23.803
Meanwhile Peter and Phyllis ran to a farm to get help.

27
00:01:24.803 --> 00:01:28.846
When the two children arrived with some farmers, they found Bobbie and Jim asleep.

28
00:01:29.046 --> 00:01:31.088
The farmers carried Jim on a plank of wood.

29
00:01:32.364 --> 00:01:33.205
"Where does he live?"

30
00:01:33.605 --> 00:01:34.226
asked a farmer.

31
00:01:34.246 --> 00:01:37.608
"In Northumberland," answered Bobbie.

32
00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:40.170
"He told me while we were waiting.

33
00:01:41.171 --> 00:01:42.392
Bring him to our house first.

34
00:01:43.213 --> 00:01:44.514
It's not far along the road.

35
00:01:45.455 --> 00:01:47.136
I'm sure Mother will say it's all right."

36
00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:52.821
Mother did say it was all right, although she was surprised.

37
00:01:52.841 --> 00:01:58.565
"I'm sorry to be so much trouble," Jim said to Mother as the men carried him in.

38
00:01:59.726 --> 00:02:01.448
His face was still white with pain.

39
00:02:02.908 --> 00:02:05.570
"Don't worry, dear, the doctor will come soon."

40
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.952
Mother also sent a message to Jim's school to tell them what had happened.

41
00:02:11.493 --> 00:02:13.994
"My grandfather lives near here," said Jim.

42
00:02:14.014 --> 00:02:17.136
"I'll write and tell him," said Mother.

43
00:02:19.297 --> 00:02:21.278
The next day someone knocked at the front door.

44
00:02:21.298 --> 00:02:24.580
"That'll be the doctor again," said Mother.

45
00:02:25.861 --> 00:02:26.901
But it wasn't the doctor.

46
00:02:27.702 --> 00:02:29.603
The children recognized the visitor's voice.

47
00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.324
But who was it?

48
00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.641
Then Mother called out, "Jim's grandfather has come.

49
00:02:36.702 --> 00:02:37.922
He wants to see you all."

50
00:02:38.942 --> 00:02:43.364
They followed Mother into the front room, and there was the old gentleman!

51
00:02:43.384 --> 00:02:45.945
"Oh, it's you!"

52
00:02:46.345 --> 00:02:47.026
cried Bobbie.

53
00:02:48.106 --> 00:02:49.887
The children were excited to see him.

54
00:02:49.907 --> 00:02:54.128
"But you're not going to take Jim away, are you?

55
00:02:55.249 --> 00:02:57.950
I was hoping he could stay for a while," Peter said.

56
00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.191
The old gentleman smiled.

57
00:03:00.211 --> 00:03:02.572
"No," he said.

58
00:03:03.688 --> 00:03:05.189
"Your mother is very kind.

59
00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:08.991
Jim will stay here and she'll look after him."

60
00:03:11.212 --> 00:03:12.633
"What about Mother's writing?"

61
00:03:12.953 --> 00:03:14.774
Peter said, before anyone could stop him.

62
00:03:15.835 --> 00:03:17.896
The old gentleman smiled kindly at Mother.

63
00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:22.378
"She can stop writing, and there will be enough food," he said.

64
00:03:22.398 --> 00:03:27.261
"Bobbie," said the old man, "can you show me to the door?"

65
00:03:28.561 --> 00:03:30.743
The old gentleman and Bobbie walked outside.

66
00:03:30.763 --> 00:03:34.641
"I received your letter, Bobbie, but it wasn't necessary.

67
00:03:35.822 --> 00:03:37.523
I had already read the newspaper.

68
00:03:38.723 --> 00:03:39.764
I tried to help him.

69
00:03:40.665 --> 00:03:42.986
I haven't done much, but I have hope."

70
00:03:43.006 --> 00:03:47.429
"Oh!" said Bobbie, crying a little.

71
00:03:47.449 --> 00:03:51.011
"But keep your secret a little longer," he said.

72
00:03:51.031 --> 00:03:54.033
"You don't think Father did it, do you?"

73
00:03:54.453 --> 00:03:54.994
said Bobbie.

74
00:03:55.014 --> 00:03:58.576
"I'm sure he didn't," said the old gentleman.
